~ start
Monk: [speed=0.5]I thought, stopping time would fix everything..
Plooy: If we never do anything, time will eventually cease to exist in this dimension.
Monk: But I am the embodiment of your mistakes. I will always choose the opposite. The cycle will never end.
Plooy: Like you said, for every choice we make, there's a timeline where it's different.
Plooy: There is a Plooy that never acts. And a Plooy that chooses to destroy.
Plooy: But what matters... is the Plooy we are at this very moment.
Monk: But the loop of disappointment will just keep repeating itself.
Plooy: The loop will never break if we choose to do nothing about it.
Plooy: What we are now is what matters... And what tomorrow becomes is our next step.
Monk: You would let Plooy make mistakes?
Plooy: [speed=0.6]As long as we face them... [speed=0.3]Together.
=> END